## Roles

The DRA has approximately 10 trustees. We have the typical charity roles: Chair, Treasurer, and Secretary, plus representatives from neighbouring organisations including Dartington Primary School, The Wave, Bidwell Brook School, and Lifeworks, as well as representatives from the clubs who use the facilities.

Trustees stand down at each Annual General Meeting (AGM), and new trustees are nominated. Meetings are open to the public; if you would like to attend, please [subscribe to the mailing list](/subscribe-to-updates).

A [trustee application form](/be-a-trustee) is available for anyone interested in becoming a trustee. These forms are circulated to trustees in the lead-up to the AGM. A good way to start is by volunteering.

## Volunteers

A pool of volunteers keep the DRA going. We need help with both ad-hoc events and day-to-day activities. Many volunteers are former trustees or are on the path to becoming trustees. If you are interested, please [subscribe to the mailing list and let us know your areas of interest](/volunteer).

## Working Groups

Currently we have several key working groups, composed of individuals who report to the trustees but also operate with autonomy:

- Pool Group: working towards the revival of the Dartington swimming pool
- Building Group: improving the existing building and scoping out the next phase of development
- Operations Group: responsible for the day-to-day management of the organisation and facilities

